  m_Name: Journal_scan_pulse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  id: journal.scan_pulse
  title: "Reading the Pulse"
  author: "Survey Lead A. Kovacs"
  dateLine: "Field note, base zone"
  category: 2
  body: "The handheld scanner sits on key 1; pulse it with the left mouse button. A pulse reports the strongest archaeological signal in range: its strength, roughly how far away it is, its bearing and its depth. Early readings are rough.\n\nDon't stand in one spot pulsing at the sand. Pulse, walk a good distance sideways, and pulse again: the fix tightens as you triangulate. Get close enough and the site pinpoints and gets marked. While the scanner is out, a gold chevron at the edge of your crosshair points to the nearest site.\n\nA reading of VALUABLE SIGNATURE is a cache, not a dig site. More on those elsewhere."
  placement: 2
  bodyId: 
  siteIndex: 0
  order: 11
